{"name":"Cosmic Explorer","hex":"#551155","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cosmic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or from or pertaining to the cosmos or universe.","Characteristic of the cosmos or universe; inconceivably great; vast."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cosmic"},{"term":"explorer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who explores something","A person who by means of travel (notably an expedition) searches out new information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/explorer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cosmic Explorer","blocks":[{"text":"Cosmic Explorer is the fifth studio album by Japanese girl group Perfume. It was released on April 6, 2016 by Universal Music Japan, Universal J, and Perfume Records. It is Perfume's fifth consecutive album to be fully produced, written, composed, and arranged by Japanese musician and Capsule band member Yasutaka Nakata. Five different formats were released to promote the album: a standalone CD, a double CD and DVD/Blu-ray box set, a digital release and a double disc vinyl, where the first disc is blue and the second disc could be orange, pink or yellow. The vinyls were available for purchase at Perfume: A Gallery Experience Supported by Rhizomatiks in London and NY."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fd/Perfumecosmicexplorer.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmic_Explorer","wikidata":"Q23057910"},{"title":"Cosmic Explorer (gravitational wave observatory)","blocks":[{"text":"Cosmic Explorer (CE) is a proposed next-generation ground-based gravitational wave observatory. It will consist of two L-shaped interferometers, similar to the LIGO detectors, but with significantly increased arm length that aims to increase the sensitivity of CE by more than an order of magnitude with respect to the 4-km long LIGO. It is planned to complement its proposed European counterpart, Einstein Telescope (ET), with a similar timeline."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Cosmic_Explorer_-_Off_Campus_Daytime_Visualization.jpg/330px-Cosmic_Explorer_-_Off_Campus_Daytime_Visualization.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmic_Explorer_(gravitational_wave_observatory)","wikidata":"Q85754182"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fd/Perfumecosmicexplorer.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fd/Perfumecosmicexplorer.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APerfumecosmicexplorer.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Cosmic_Explorer_-_Off_Campus_Daytime_Visualization.jpg/500px-Cosmic_Explorer_-_Off_Campus_Daytime_Visualization.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Cosmic_Explorer_-_Off_Campus_Daytime_Visualization.jpg/1280px-Cosmic_Explorer_-_Off_Campus_Daytime_Visualization.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Cosmic_Explorer_-_Off_Campus_Daytime_Visualization.jpg/500px-Cosmic_Explorer_-_Off_Campus_Daytime_Visualization.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACosmic_Explorer_-_Off_Campus_Daytime_Visualization.jpg"}],"sounds":{"cosmic":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/38/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-cosmic.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.